      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that \\(a = 3b\\), \\(b = 2c\\), and \\(c = 4d\\), we need to find the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\).\n\nFirst, substitute the expressions for \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) in terms of \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\na = 3b = 3(2c) = 3 \\cdot 2c = 6c\n\\]\n\n\\[\nb = 2c\n\\]\n\n\\[\nc = 4d\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(c = 4d\\) into the expression for \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\na = 6c = 6(4d) = 24d\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(b = 2c\\) and \\(c = 4d\\) into the expression for \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\nb = 2c = 2(4d) = 8d\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(a = 24d\\), \\(b = 8d\\), and \\(c = 4d\\) into the expression \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d} = \\frac{(24d) \\cdot (4d)}{(8d) \\cdot d}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{24d \\cdot 4d}{8d \\cdot d} = \\frac{96d^2}{8d^2}\n\\]\n\nCancel out \\(d^2\\) from the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{96d^2}{8d^2} = \\frac{96}{8} = 12\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
