      "text": "Given that \\( a = 3b \\), \\( b = 2c \\), and \\( c = 4d \\), we need to find the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\).\n\nFirst, express \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) in terms of \\(d\\):\n\\[ a = 3b \\]\n\\[ b = 2c \\]\n\\[ c = 4d \\]\n\nSubstitute \\(c = 4d\\) into the equation for \\(b\\):\n\\[ b = 2c = 2(4d) = 8d \\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(b = 8d\\) into the equation for \\(a\\):\n\\[ a = 3b = 3(8d) = 24d \\]\n\nNow, we have:\n\\[ a = 24d \\]\n\\[ b = 8d \\]\n\\[ c = 4d \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d} = \\frac{(24d) \\cdot (4d)}{(8d) \\cdot d} = \\frac{96d^2}{8d^2} = \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\]\n\nThus, the value is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
