    "text": "Given that \\(a\\) is three times \\(b\\), we can write:\n\\[ a = 3b \\]\n\nNext, we know that \\(b\\) is twice \\(c\\), so:\n\\[ b = 2c \\]\n\nAnd \\(c\\) is four times \\(d\\), so:\n\\[ c = 4d \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\). First, substitute the expressions for \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) in terms of \\(d\\).\n\nStarting with \\(a\\):\n\\[ a = 3b = 3(2c) = 3(2(4d)) = 3 \\cdot 8d = 24d \\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) into the expression \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d} = \\frac{(24d) \\cdot (4d)}{(2c) \\cdot d} = \\frac{96d^2}{2cd} = \\frac{96d^2}{2cd} = \\frac{96d}{2c} = \\frac{96d}{2(4d)} = \\frac{96d}{8d} = \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\]\n\nThus, the value is:\n\\[ \\boxed{12} \\]",
